[Figure: Right triangle ABC with right angle at C. Vertex A at top, vertex B at bottom right, vertex C at bottom left. Hypotenuse AB = 54, angle B = 30^\circ. Note: Figure not drawn to scale.]

Right triangle ABC is shown. What is the value of \tan A?
A. \frac{\sqrt{3}}{54}
B. \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}
C. \sqrt{3}
D. 27\sqrt{3}

The perimeter of an isosceles right triangle is 18 + 18\sqrt{2} inches. What is the length, in inches, of the hypotenuse of this triangle?
A. 9
B. 9\sqrt{2}
C. 18
D. 18\sqrt{2}
